{
  "version": 2,
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": "markup",
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": [
        "# Zig\n",
        "\n",
        "Zig is the case that proves the argument builder has to be per-language: there\n",
        "is no `-o`. The command line is `zig build-exe main.zig --name greeter` — a\n",
        "subcommand, and the binary named by a flag.\n",
        "\n",
        "Like Rust, `zig` is pointed at **one root file**; the cell below it is written\n",
        "into the build dir and reached with `@import`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "toml",
      "value": [
        "# Defaults for a zig project: the `zig` compiler, no flags (Debug).\n",
        "# Add e.g. flags = [\"-OReleaseFast\"] to change that.\n",
        "mode   = \"run\"\n",
        "output = \"greeter\"\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "zig",
      "value": [
        "const std = @import(\"std\");\n",
        "\n",
        "pub const names = [_][]const u8{ \"world\", \"zig\" };\n",
        "\n",
        "/// Builds the greeting. Zig has no hidden allocator, so a function that\n",
        "/// returns a new string has to be handed one — and the caller owns the result.\n",
        "pub fn greeting(gpa: std.mem.Allocator, name: []const u8) ![]u8 {\n",
        "    return std.fmt.allocPrint(gpa, \"hello, {s}, from a compiler notebook\", .{name});\n",
        "}\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "role": "file",
        "filename": "greeter.zig"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "markup",
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": [
        "`@import(\"greeter.zig\")` resolves against the build directory, so the import\n",
        "string and the file name on the cell above have to match.\n",
        "\n",
        "`std.process.Init` is where the entry point gets its allocator and its I/O — the\n",
        "cell below passes the arena to `greeting` and lets it go out of scope at the end\n",
        "of `main`.\n",
        "\n",
        "> Written against zig 0.17-dev, whose `std.Io` is still moving. On an older\n",
        "> toolchain, take the allocator from a `std.heap.GeneralPurposeAllocator` and\n",
        "> print with `std.debug.print(\"{s}\\n\", .{line})` instead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "zig",
      "value": [
        "const std = @import(\"std\");\n",
        "const greeter = @import(\"greeter.zig\");\n",
        "\n",
        "pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !void {\n",
        "    // The arena is freed when main returns, so the greetings need no defer.\n",
        "    const gpa = init.arena.allocator();\n",
        "\n",
        "    var buf: [256]u8 = undefined;\n",
        "    var out = std.Io.File.stdout().writerStreaming(init.io, &buf);\n",
        "\n",
        "    for (greeter.names) |name| {\n",
        "        const line = try greeter.greeting(gpa, name);\n",
        "        try out.interface.print(\"{s}\\n\", .{line});\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    try out.flush();\n",
        "}\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "role": "file",
        "filename": "main.zig"
      }
    }
  ]
}
